                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="org_143">Cirencester, Gloucestershire.
                        Augustinian abbey of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>The table of contents
                        in Prise's hand suggests that this may be from Cirencester, as such notes
                        are found regularly in the Cirencester manuscripts at Jesus and Hereford,
                        but rarely in any manuscripts owned by Prise and coming from religious
                        houses other than Cirencester. The rubrics to the works of Ambrose and
                        Gregory of Nazianzus in this manuscript match those used in the Registrum
                        Anglie (R3.1; R18.2, 13, 14), reporting copies at Cirencester, and might
                        also have caused its misattribution of the ‘Expositio baptisterii’ to
                        Gregory (correctly Leidrad, De sacramento baptismi).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sir John Prise (1501/2--1555).</provenance>
               </history>
